; Converting between the two wide types, which only i128 being a machine type of
; its own makes possible: one register is half of a pair, so the conversions are
; subregister moves rather than the limb arithmetic the other configuration has
; to fall back on. Both are pinned here, so the difference the option makes is
; visible in one place.

; The wide value is computed, so the truncation is a real one rather than a
; narrower load the combiner folded.
